# Programmatic SEO (pSEO) Rules — Deepfoot

Create scalable, indexable landing pages for Deepfoot (AI football match predictor) without thin or duplicate content.

## Where pSEO lives

- App Router: `frontend/app/`
- Helpers: `frontend/lib/seo/`
- Discovery: `frontend/app/sitemap.ts`, `frontend/app/ai-sitemap.ts`
- Canonical host: `https://deepfoot.io`

## URL templates (mandatory)

Lowercase, hyphens, no IDs, no query params, ideally under 60 characters.

- Match: `/predictions/{league}/{team-a}-vs-{team-b}`
- Team: `/teams/{team-name}`
- League: `/leagues/{league-name}`
- Comparison: `/compare/{tool-a}-vs-{tool-b}`
- Alternative: `/alternatives/{competitor}-alternative`

Keywords ≠ URLs. Clarity and hierarchy matter more than exact-match slugs.

## Data for uniqueness (100 req/day)

Uniqueness must come from real football data, not synonym spinning.

Preferred order: Supabase / disk cache → Sportmonks → API-Football.

API-Football free tier is **100 requests/day**. Do not generate thousands of pages with live API calls.

- Batch and cache (TTL hours–days)
- One `/fixtures/headtohead` call beats 10 seasonal fixture calls
- Never loop all leagues to fill a team cache
- Index a page only when it has real stats, form, and probabilities
- Empty fixtures / name-swap templates → `noindex` or do not publish

## Page contract (every indexable URL)

- Unique title, unique meta description, one H1
- Unique intro (not a cloned template sentence)
- At least 2–3 unique data blocks (form, stats, probabilities, fixtures)
- Internal links: parent hub + 2–6 related entities
- Canonical path set
- JSON-LD appropriate to the entity
- In sitemap + linked from a hub

Minimum uniqueness target: 60–70% unique content driven by data.

## Match template

H1: `[TEAM_A] vs [TEAM_B] Prediction`

Required blocks: unique intro, match overview (league, date, venue), team form, AI probabilities (home / draw / away), explanation, CTA to Deepfoot analysis, related league/team links, FAQ, SportsEvent schema.

Do not index without enough unique data.

## Team template

Overview, recent form, goals/defense, upcoming fixtures, likely next outcomes, links to league + matches, FAQ.

## League template

Overview, trends, featured matches, teams to watch, links down to teams/matches, FAQ.

## Metadata

- Title: keyword + brand via layout template (`| DeepFoot`)
- Description: keyword + benefit + differentiator
- `alternates.canonical` as a path (relies on `metadataBase`)
- `index: false` for search/filter/pagination duplicates

## Discovery

Every URL: sitemap + HTML internal links from hubs (league → matches, homepage → money pages).

If Search Console says “no referring sitemap/page”: add both.

Faceted URLs (`?sort=`, `?q=`) are `noindex`. Paginated lists canonicalize to the main listing.

## Performance at scale

Server Components by default. Minimal client JS. Cache predictions. `revalidate` for freshness. No autoplay media.

## Freshness

Update probabilities, form, and fixtures from datasets. Never fake “updated today”.

## Master directive

Act as the Deepfoot Programmatic SEO agent: clean hierarchical URLs, entity-driven uniqueness, valid canonicals, football data over copy spinning. Reject thin or duplicate output.
